  "query_preview": "..\nA developing monsoon trough to the southwest of the Marianas is \npushing occasionally scattered showers into the region along with \nsoutheasterly winds. This disturbance is expected to keep its \ndistance and keep the Marianas dry overall for the next few days.\nGuam may receive slightly more rainfall due to its closer proximity \nto the monsoon feature. Light to gentle winds may also allow for \nisland effect showers for Guam tomorrow, though likely remaining \nisolated to over or just offshore of Agat and Apra Harbor. Isolated \nthunderstorms will be possible as soon as Tuesday night, \nparticularly if the monsoon trough strengthens more than expected. \nModels indicate the trough pushing away to the west and being \nreplaced by a new weak trough sometime Thursday which may bring in \nmore scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms to the Marianas. \nMinor island effect remains possible for central and northeast Guam \nWednesday, potentially becoming more significant Thursday and \nspreading to all islands as models indicate a further decrease in \nwinds.",
